# TutorKeyBox02: Product Vision Board & Architectural Blueprint

> **High-Performance Hybrid Piano Synthesizer**  
> *Mac Studio/Laptop Editor & Remote Controller + Raspberry Pi 5 Ultra-Low Latency Embedded Audio Engine*

---

## 1. Product Vision & Concept

TutorKeyBox is an ultra-low-latency, multi-layer sample-playback synthesizer designed for professional live performance and sound design.

```
+------------------------------------+          UDP Telemetry (200ms)         +------------------------------------+
|            macOS GUI App           | <------------------------------------> |       Raspberry Pi 5 Daemon        |
|  - Standalone Local Sound Preview  |                                        |  - Headless ALSA Audio Core        |
|  - Layer Mute/Gain Editing         | ------ TCP Hardware Preset Deploy ---> |  - 64-sample Buffer (~1.3ms)       |
|  - Drag & Drop Sample Packaging    |               (Port 7778)              |  - Zero-Heap Allocation SIMD DSP   |
+------------------------------------+                                        +------------------------------------+
```

### Core Value Propositions
1. **Zero-Latency Playback:** Raspberry Pi 5 runs headless direct ALSA output with ARM NEON SIMD sample interpolation.
2. **Offline Mac Sound Design:** Sound design happens on Mac with zero network dependency. Press **Deploy** to push presets to hardware.
3. **Hard Power-Cut Resilience:** Memory-mapped read-only `.bin` container streaming ensures SD card power cuts never corrupt sample files.

